# Path-scoped VPS deploy

Site Deploy workflows (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) must gate CI steps by **changed paths**. Do not rebuild, upload, or restart unused slices on every push to `main`.

## Required scopes

| Scope | Paths (example) | CI must |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Frontend | `frontend/**` | Build Astro + rsync `frontend/dist/` → `/var/www/<domain>/html/` only |
| Backend | `backend/**` except heavy data packs | `go test`, Linux AMD64 `api`, release switch, **restart API** + health check |
| Data packs | e.g. `backend/.data/calvin-institutes-paragraphs/**` | rsync that pack only; **no** API restart unless backend code also changed |

If none of those paths changed (docs, rules, workflow-only fixes that do not need a release), skip SSH uploads and restarts — job may exit after scope resolution.

Manual **`workflow_dispatch`**: deploy all scopes (full rebuild).

## Detection

- Prefer `git diff --name-only $BEFORE $AFTER` (checkout `fetch-depth: 0`) with an explicit `case` on paths.
- Do **not** rely on `dorny/paths-filter` negation patterns with default `predicate-quantifier: some` — `!path/**` falsely matches unrelated files.
- Order matters: match pack paths **before** the broad `backend/*` branch.

## Agent rules when editing deploy.yml

- Keep FE-only pushes fast: no Go setup/tests/compile, no pack rsync, no `systemctl restart`.
- Never reintroduce unconditional Calvin (or other large pack) sync on every deploy.
- Never restart the API when only frontend or only a static data pack changed.
- Align new site deploys with this pattern (see `github-vps-deploy-secrets.mdc` for SSH secret names).

```text
❌ BAD: every main push → npm build + go test + calvin rsync + systemctl restart
✅ GOOD: frontend-only → npm build + rsync html/
✅ GOOD: backend-only → go test/build + release + restart
✅ GOOD: calvin-pack-only → rsync pack (no restart)
```
